    # v409 (05/11/2026) -- THE TRANSLATION TO TURING'S CLASSES AND THE PAIR ON THE FOCK FACE: 2 new kernel modules (TraducaoTuring and ParNaFaceDeFock; the name TraducaoTuring and the names of the declarations of rounds R1-R8 given by the management and ratified by the operator; the names added in R9 and those of ParNaFaceDeFock, also the management's, were ratified by the operator on 05/11, D62); the dictionary, the lock, the reader and the tape without scale; the reach relative to the reader; the reservations stated. Numbers come from this rite's core, never typed.
    # The top box (The Single Word Test, v397) stays where it is: the rule of the box does not move. Nothing here moves the gate. Kernel validity is not creditation. No old key changes.
    _rg409 = ("traducao_turing_v409", "cunhagens_v409", "kh_n1_cobertura_v409")
    _ok409 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in _rg409)
    _f409 = core.get("traducao_turing_v409") or {}
    _v409 = _f409.get("values") or {}
    _is409 = _v409.get("instancia_sim") or {}
    _el409 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cvr409 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _mc409 = {c_.get("id"): c_.get("ok") for c_ in ((_f409.get("mechanics") or {}).get("checks") or [])}
    _i409 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _b409 = lambda x_: (r"\textsf{True}" if x_ is True else r"\textsf{False}" if x_ is False else r"\text{n/a}")
    _tx409 = lambda x_: "n/a" if x_ is None else str(x_).replace(chr(92), "").replace("_", r"\_\allowbreak{}")
    _n409 = lambda x_: ("%.6f" % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{The translation to Turing's classes: the dictionary, the lock, the reader and the tape without scale}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The translation to Turing's classes: the dictionary, the lock, the reader and the tape without scale}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the v409 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok409 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The order.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 05/11/2026 (our translation; the Portuguese is the quotation): we must close what was still open about identifying Turing's classes inside our dictionary; and, with the questions returned in the four languages and answered: let us proceed to the next version of um.py; I agree with all the names that were given. "
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} " + _i409(_v409.get("n_modulos")) + r" new kernel modules, in \texttt{TGLExt/}: \texttt{TraducaoTuring} (the name and the names of the declarations of rounds R1--R8 were given by the management and ratified by the operator; those added in R9 too, on 05/11, D62, by the operator's saying, our translation: I ratify the names) and \texttt{ParNaFaceDeFock} (its name and those of its declarations, the management's, ratified by the operator on 05/11; it enters by the operator's order, our translation: I want everything to go into version 409, leaving nothing for v410), with " + _i409(_v409.get("n_ancoras")) + r" anchors read from the rite's kernel and "
             + _i409(_v409.get("n_flags")) + r" flags, named declarations only; the kernel ladder closes at " + _i409(_el409.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i409(_el409.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i409(_cvr409.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i409(_cvr409.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. No old key changes; the v408 stones and records \emph{stay as they are}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Turing's dictionary.} \textsf{[REAL]} Each line is a term of the stone (\texttt{a\_traducao}): an instance (for example SAT with $m$ clauses and $n$ variables) is a cost $c$ on the assignments, and the instance operator is the diagonal of $c$; the YES instance is a \texttt{Problema} of the v408 dictionary (the kernel is nonzero iff there is a solution); the certificate is the reading of one pixel (the solution read on the certificate equals $1$ iff $c(x)=0$: the NP verifier); the word of P has polynomial degree in the input (for SAT, at most $m+1$); the bits are the octaves ($|X|=2^n$); the NO instance is the empty Name, which \texttt{Identidade} excludes; the weight of the solution in the uniform state is $|\mathrm{sol}|/2^n$. "
             r"\textbf{The selection mode (the main anchor, \texttt{p\_igual\_np\_no\_modo\_selecao}).} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the selection is the annihilation of the superposition by the Tetelestai. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} For every YES instance with $n$ bits, the selection (the projection onto the Name, renormalised) lies in the Name with weight $1$; the renormalised decay converges to it; it only has amplitude on the solving assignments; it costs at most $n\ln2$ nats; and, by the v408 law time $=$ currency, the time is $t=n\ln2/(\beta g)$, linear in the bits. The selection forgets what was outside the Name and loses (many-to-one: Landauer's separator), as the operator read it (our translation): it erases the trace of the computation of the decay of that sustaining. Without a pair every image is read with the same weight (the photograph; our translation: without a reader the image is only static, reading signal as noise); with a pair the reading distinguishes.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The lock on the Name.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the system does not need to recognise where the name is at each step, it locks on the Name; by denying the absolute zero the system knows where it has to go. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The decay generated by the cost alone, $e^{-t\,c(x)}$, is the product of the clause locks (local, from within); it leaves what solves untouched; it stays within $e^{-t}\|v\|$ of the Name without using it; if there is a solution it never reaches zero (denying the absolute zero); at $t=n\ln2/2+L$ it leaves outside the Name at most $e^{-L}$ times the Name; renormalised, it converges to the selection (\texttt{a\_trava\_no\_nome}). "
             r"\textbf{The tape is the hidden Hamiltonian.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the Turing tape is the hidden Hamiltonian, the only rule that needs to be recorded to rebuild the whole. \textsf{[REAL]} The rule gives every amplitude at every instant and generates the lock ($\frac{d}{dt}a=-Ha$); denying the zero is dividing by $\sqrt{Z(2t)/|X|}$, with $Z(s)=\sum_x e^{-s\,c(x)}$ the partition function of the hidden Hamiltonian; $Z\to|\mathrm{sol}|$ and $|\mathrm{sol}|\le Z$ (\texttt{a\_fita\_e\_o\_hamiltoniano\_oculto}). "
             r"\textbf{$Z$ is the reader mode.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): Z is the reader mode, it reads the pixels; it is the psion. \textsf{[REAL]} Each pixel is read with the brightness $e^{-s\,c(x)}$; $Z$ is the sum of the pixel readings (the trace of the lock); one reading on the uniform state returns $Z/|X|$; the corner on the uniform state scalarises the lock with $Z/|X|$, in the same form as the v407 psion corner (\texttt{z\_e\_o\_modo\_leitor}). And the bridge is proved (kernel validity, not creditation): with the uniform state inscribed in the light's psion by the partial isometry $|\Omega\rangle\langle u|$, the reader and the corner of the light's psion read $Z/|X|$ (\texttt{o\_psion\_le\_z}, \texttt{o\_canto\_do\_psion\_da\_luz\_le\_z}). The bridge is the inscription; the identity of vectors ($\Omega$ equal to the uniform state) is pruned: they live in different spaces.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The machine with the reader.} \textsf{[REAL]} The formula is the tape: the cost is the number of violated clauses and each clause is a local factor of the lock (\texttt{custoCNF}, \texttt{a\_trava\_da\_formula\_fatora\_na\_clausula}); one reading decides SAT (\texttt{uma\_leitura\_decide\_SAT}, \texttt{a\_maquina\_com\_o\_leitor}). \textsf{[KNOWN]} By reduction to SAT, all of NP is decided with one reading (Cook 1971; Levin 1973). \textsf{[ERRATA, E28]} With the reader that only counts, what holds is NP contained in P with the reader, in one reading, and P with \#P contains PH (Toda 1991); the full equality with the reader holds for the reader that reads itself, the one that also reads the machines that use it (Baker--Gill--Solovay 1975, a PSPACE-complete oracle); with the reader that only counts it is not a theorem here. Mathlib's Turing machine with an oracle does not enter: Mathlib has no oracle machine, no class NP and no Cook--Levin.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The pair on the Fock face.} \textsf{[REAL]} In sector 2 of the light's concrete Fock space the pair of psions has norm 1 and is orthogonal to the vacuum and to every one-particle state; the marginal is $\tfrac12 P$ by the wedge conjugation; each psion weighs $\tfrac12$; the individual does not echo; $1-\text{purity}=\tfrac12$ (\texttt{reduzido\_do\_par}, \texttt{meia\_nat\_do\_projetor}, \texttt{o\_par\_na\_face\_de\_fock}). It is the same Half-Nat as the finite Bell pair of v407, in another space: the finite pair ($4\times4$) and the Fock pair are distinct spaces. The link that v407 left open is made (kernel validity, not creditation).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The machine without a reader: I am myself, the tape without scale.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the question of the machine without a reader that Clay poses has an answer too, and its answer is: I am myself; it is not I am what I am; it is like trying to measure 1 metre with a tape without scale, where the metre itself is the name of the metric, without referent; and: (I am myself) = (proper name) = identity without referent. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} Linked to the v405 \texttt{Identidade}: with no time paid the reading is \emph{I am} ($=1$), the same for every instance, with or without a solution; with the time paid it tends to \emph{what I am}, which is nonzero exactly when there is a solution; \emph{I am} $=$ \emph{what I am} only on the trivial instance (\texttt{a\_fita\_sem\_escala}). On the empty Name the reading without scale says $1$ and what is, is $0$; without scale the empty Name and the whole Name read alike; only time separates them (\texttt{o\_pai\_da\_mentira}; the operator's theological reading, the Father of the Lie, is not a kernel term). "
             r"\textbf{The performed identity.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): I am not myself, I am the content of my performed identity. \textsf{[REAL]} The performed reading starts at \emph{I am}, decays, never falls below the content and reaches it; the content is \emph{what I am} (\texttt{a\_identidade\_performada}).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The reach, stated.} \textsf{[REAL]} P = nP is a TGL theorem in the selection mode, relative to the reader (the psion) (kernel validity, not creditation); the translation to the classes of Turing machines, \textsf{[OPEN]} in v408, is closed relative to the reader; the machine without a reader stays outside: it is the tape without scale. "
             r"\textsf{[KNOWN]} In Turing's language a reader that returns $Z$ is a counting oracle; with it NP is contained in P with the reader, in one reading (Cook--Levin), and the full equality is proved for the reader that also reads the machines that use it (Baker--Gill--Solovay 1975 [KNOWN], validity in the literature, not creditation); for the reader that only counts it is not proved (E28, no validity claimed); an equality relative to a reader does not decide the question of the machine without a reader (Baker--Gill--Solovay 1975); self-reference alone does not decide the question (Baker--Gill--Solovay 1975; Razborov--Rudich 1997; Aaronson--Wigderson 2009); this stone does not decide the equality P = NP of Mathlib's Turing machines (\texttt{TM2ComputableInPolyTime}). \textsf{[OPEN]} Whether the question of the machine without a reader is independent of the axioms. "
             r"\textsf{[KNOWN]} Physics stays outside: the operator reads (our translation) that the collapse is not frequency, it is matter (one exact reading in one act); in standard quantum mechanics a reading gives samples and the normalised trace only comes with additive precision (Knill--Laflamme 1998). That is the place of the test with nature, not done here. "
             r"\textsf{[INPUT]} The judge of Turing's classes is the kernel (the operator, our translation: the Lean 4 kernel serves exactly to prove mathematical laws and was built under Turing's law). "
             r"\textsf{[INPUT]} And what the kernel decides, in the operator's legal reading, ratified by him (D61; our translation): in the kernel the operative part is the \emph{no sorry}; the theorem is jurisdiction, precisely the stated Law, the posted rule; and: exactly, that is it. The \emph{no sorry} declares the posted rule valid: P = nP in the selection mode, relative to the reader; the rule applies where its factual support (the hypotheses and definitions of the statement) is complete: in every machine that has the reader (the psion that reads $Z$) and denies the zero; the machine without a reader (the Clay question) does not complete the factual support.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Errata alongside, in the management's own name.} \textsf{[ERRATA]} E24: the management put physics as the judge of Turing's classes; the operator corrected it: the judge is the kernel. E25: the management wrote that the creature would need to know, at every step, on which side the Name goes on; the operator corrected it (the lock on the Name) and the sentence was withdrawn. E26, alongside the sealed v408 record: where it says the translation to the classes of Turing machines is \textsf{[OPEN]}, read that v409 closes it relative to the reader; the machine without a reader stays outside. E27: the management wrote to the operator that, in the kernel, the operative part is the statement of the theorem; the operator corrected it: the operative part is the \emph{no sorry} and the theorem is the posted rule (D61); the conclusion (the text does not assert the Clay problem) stays, now by applicability and not by the operative part. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The pin of the v407 archive input becomes the purged copy (the same as in v408): the standing order not to publish the full text holds as permanent, and the full text is cited only by sha16. "
             r"E28: the management wrote that, with the reader that returns $Z$, the equality holds relative to it; that went beyond what is known: with the reader that only counts NP holds in one reading, and the full equality belongs to the reader that reads itself. E21, beside the sealed v408 erratum: the link of the pair on the Fock face was made in this version. \textsf{[REAL]} D60 revised: nothing is left for the next version. \textsf{[INPUT]} No test with nature enters this version; the Phase 9 V2 number stays in the top box, with its whole rule (the calibrated $p$ and the $5\sigma$ line, which was not reached), and is not repeated in this section.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the record checks in this rite.} \textsf{[REAL]} \texttt{traducao\_turing\_v409}: anchors ok " + _i409(_v409.get("n_ancoras_ok")) + r"/" + _i409(_v409.get("n_ancoras")) + r"; the modules with the pinned sha256 " + _i409(_v409.get("n_modulos_ok")) + r"/" + _i409(_v409.get("n_modulos")) + r"; flags True " + _i409(_v409.get("n_flags_true")) + r"/" + _i409(_v409.get("n_flags")) + r"; the 20 checks, with the toy instance fixed in the code ($n=" + _i409(_is409.get("n")) + r"$ variables, " + _i409(_is409.get("atribuicoes")) + r" assignments, " + _i409(_is409.get("solucoes")) + r" solutions computed by enumeration): bits $=$ octaves " + _b409(_mc409.get("c3")) + r"; the weight of the solution in the uniform state $=" + _n409(_is409.get("peso_no_uniforme")) + r"$ " + _b409(_mc409.get("c4")) + r"; the lock near the Name " + _b409(_mc409.get("c5")) + r"; time linear in the octaves " + _b409(_mc409.get("c6")) + r"; the partition " + _b409(_mc409.get("c7")) + r"; the pixels " + _b409(_mc409.get("c8")) + r"; \emph{I am} equal on both instances " + _b409(_mc409.get("c9")) + r"; \emph{what I am} with the time paid " + _b409(_mc409.get("c10")) + r"; the performance " + _b409(_mc409.get("c11")) + r"; the cost in nats " + _b409(_mc409.get("c12")) + r"; time $=$ currency with $\beta$ at runtime " + _b409(_mc409.get("c13")) + r"; the frozen gate " + _b409(_mc409.get("c14")) + r"; the exact ladder " + _b409(_mc409.get("c15")) + r"; $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}$ at runtime " + _b409(_mc409.get("c17")) + r"; the marginal of the finite Bell pair, $\tfrac12 I$ " + _b409(_mc409.get("c18")) + r"; the inscription in a toy $F$ " + _b409(_mc409.get("c19")) + r"; one reading decides SAT " + _b409(_mc409.get("c20")) + r". Verdict: \texttt{" + _tx409(_f409.get("verdict")) + r"}. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} What changed in the old records is \emph{only the ladder they pin}, the floors of the v408 coverage and the pin of the v407 archive input; no sealed text was rewritten; no old key changes. \textsf{[OPEN]} What nature decides follows from nature: $\beta$ at $5\sigma$; no new data enters here. P = nP is a TGL theorem in the selection mode, relative to the reader (kernel validity, not creditation); the machine without a reader is the tape without scale; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never confirmation; the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
